      "statement_id": "P3.CyclicSymbiosis",
      "statement_sha256": "a6825700fb4c21d12ba330c739d321dd105da3b21c394338cda11ef5a67667c4",
      "text": "For every N >= 2 and all costs c, values v : Fin N -> R with every c i > 0 and v i > 0, there exists a flow x with every x i > 0 and every net benefit v i * x (prev i) - c i * x i > 0 (prev i = (i + N - 1) mod N) if and only if the product of the c i is strictly less than the product of the v i.",
      "trivial": false
    },
    "C2": {
      "kind": "conjecture",
      "label": "ASSUMED",
      "reason": "conjecture",
      "text": "For a general strongly connected exchange network with linear separable payoffs, a strictly beneficial positive flow exists iff a cycle-product (spectral-type) condition on the per-link value/cost ratios holds. This generalises the simple-cycle result; it is not stated precisely or proved here."
    }
  },
